    "deck": "A 156.32-point eruption reset the Golden High Point, while schedule strength and all-play performance expose which records are sturdy and which may be living dangerously.",
    "story": [
      "Turbulent Ticklesh!ts delivered the defining score of Week 4, crushing the slate with 156.32 points and establishing the season’s new Golden High Point. The total was 19.10 points clear of the week’s runner-up, California Un-Named Team, and pushed Ticklesh!ts to 522.76 points through four weeks, the most in the GFL.",
      "The standings are beginning to separate from the underlying performance."The standings are beginning to separate from the underlying performance. California Un-Named Team remains the league's lone undefeated team at 4-0, while Sullco MethMouths sits among a group of strong 3-1 contenders. The scoring race, however, still points to Turbulent Ticklesh!ts as the league's most dangerous weekly ceiling. Meanwhile, Off Boys has quietly stacked 462.08 points and remains firmly in the contender conversation after a 131.16-point outburst in Week 4.",
      "Schedule context matters. Medford MountainMen has faced the strongest slate so far by opponent winning percentage (0.750), while Turbulent Ticklesh!ts has drawn the lightest (0.188). That does not erase wins or losses, but it gives the early records a better frame.",
